Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Mochi links against third-party Rust crates at build time. Every dependency is
required by CI (see deny.toml) to be distributed under a permissive licence:
Apache-2.0, MIT, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, Zlib, Unicode-3.0 or
Unlicense. Copyleft licences (GPL / LGPL / AGPL / MPL) are rejected.

The bundled SQLite amalgamation reached through `libsqlite3-sys` is in the
public domain (https://www.sqlite.org/copyright.html).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Mozilla Public License 2.0 components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The desktop application reaches these crates through Tauri and uses them
unmodified. MPL-2.0 asks that recipients be told where to obtain their source;
each is published on crates.io under the name and version recorded in
Cargo.lock, and their repositories are linked from there.

  option-ext    (via dirs)        https://crates.io/crates/option-ext
  cssparser     (build time only) https://crates.io/crates/cssparser
  cssparser-macros                https://crates.io/crates/cssparser-macros
  selectors                       https://crates.io/crates/selectors
  dtoa-short                      https://crates.io/crates/dtoa-short

Should Mochi ever modify one of these, the modified files remain under MPL-2.0
and must be published as such.

A machine-generated inventory of the exact dependency versions and their
licences is produced by `cargo deny list` and is published with each release.
When a new dependency introduces its own NOTICE requirements, its attribution
must be appended to this file (Apache-2.0 section 4(d)).
